ate... Return the minimum score among candidates... Does that work? Yes... Start with numerous lengths... but the number is large... In the previous program, it said to avoid using different lengths... Now, I have to avoid that because larger sequences might have larger evaluation time... I don't know the time it takes to evaluate... But the previous program said at least 0.1 seconds... and might take more for larger n... But since n is length, larger n has more convolution points... So more expensive... We must use a time budget to ensure we finish... Let's use a smaller initial population for the genetic part... Only a few lengths... Let me use 4 lengths: ones around new sizes... The values might be promising... Hopefully, computing the new score should be efficient...any case, it's the only way... I have to output the results... So on to the code...",
